From 3cabca9aebb09f13c9557b797d8f945658379c52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 11:22:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 087/122] BLOCKSCALEACTION: its connection points after those
 of the base point

AcDbBlockScaleAction has 3 connection points after the 2 of
AcDbBlockActionWithBasePt (conn_pts[5], in_dxf reads them to 2-4), but
they were read into 0-2, overwriting UpdatedBaseX and UpdatedBaseY with
Scale and XScale.

* src/dwg2.spec (BLOCKSCALEACTION): The connection points 2-4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/dwg2.spec | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/dwg2.spec b/src/dwg2.spec
index 8f8e3a6..760fe0c 100644
--- a/src/dwg2.spec
+++ b/src/dwg2.spec
@@ -3713,7 +3713,8 @@ DWG_OBJECT_END
 DWG_OBJECT (BLOCKSCALEACTION)
   AcDbBlockActionWithBasePt_fields; // lgtm[cpp/use-after-free] codeql[cpp/use-after-free]
   SUBCLASS (AcDbBlockScaleAction);
-  BlockAction_ConnectionPts (conn_pts, 0, 3, 94, 303);
+  // after the 2 of AcDbBlockActionWithBasePt
+  BlockAction_ConnectionPts (conn_pts, 2, 3, 92, 301);
   START_OBJECT_HANDLE_STREAM;
 DWG_OBJECT_END
 
